{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/751727-accessing-lairs-makes-no-sense","id":751727,"title":"Accessing Lairs makes no sense","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-03T11:02:10-08:00","id":751727,"title":"Accessing Lairs makes no sense","content":"At first, I thought it was simple enough - you open a Pathway to your Lair, travel through the pathway while its open, and then you're in your lair. When you want to leave, you open another pathway to do so.<br /> <br /> Apparently, that's not the case. You open a pathway, and it stays open for a number of turns equal to your resolve (So 2 turns, or 6 seconds for an average Beast). Afterwards, the locations split again, and you (as well as anyone you brought with you) are dumped back in the physical world as the realities separate, unless you've managed to transition to another chamber in the two turns of action you have in the Lair.<br /> <br /> Can someone explain to me how this isn't borderline useless?<br /> <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T13:01:44-08:00","id":752104,"title":"","content":"1) There are other ways of getting into your lair than forcing open the Primordial Pathway. <br /> <br /> 2) This particular way of opening the Primordial Pathway merges the local environment with your Lair - so, you fill the area with bugs, water, lava, whatever. Great way of inflicting Tilts in a fight, or potentially any other reason for such massive environmental magics.<br /> <br /> 3) You also merge with your Horror, meaning its the best way to reveal your true form to mortals, plus you get a rather significant boost to your stats while in that merged form.<br /> <br /> 4) You can still open the path so that you and others walk into the Lair in addition to the above two points. So, its <i>more useful</i> than you thought, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T14:05:44-08:00","id":752218,"title":"","content":"I'd also add that it isn't generally a good idea to assume the, &quot;Joe Schmoe Average mortal,&quot; rating is the average rating for supernaturals. Resolve is a very useful trait, and I rarely see it stay at 2 for long with PCs (assuming it doesn't start at 3 or 4 as it is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:09:10-08:00","id":752344,"title":"","content":"Also, if you get an Exceptional Success, the Pathway stays for the remainder of the scene. I thought of letting Beasts with a Lair of 3 or 4 have access to a 3 dot Merit that lets them have an Exceptional Success of the roll for opening the Pathway with 3 successes instead of 5, and ignore a penalty to the roll equal to its dot rating. You could also house rule that the dice pool to open the Pathway is [highest between Wits and Resolve] + Occult + Lair instead, thus increasing the odds of getting at least 3 successes once you have that Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T16:16:51-08:00","id":752350,"title":"","content":"The trick is to open the pathway when you're standing right next to where there's a burrow in the lair. Open, step through, close. You're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T12:13:27-08:00","id":754718,"title":"","content":"I might read it wrong, but nothing prevent the Beast to remain in her lair when the pathway close, and you may use Hold the Door to trick someone to follow you. The Resolve duration is only the time the pathway remains open. I understand however, that the text is unclear about that, but that's the way I'd play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}